    "evidence_text": "Traditional methods like Hidden Markov Model (HMM) with rule based approaches,, and Support Vector Machine (SVM) with manual feature-engineering have been applied but they perform poor compared to neural.\n\nFirst we are comparing BiLSTM, BiLSTM+CNN, BiLSTM+CRF, BiLSTM+CNN+CRF models with CNN model and Stanford CRF model.\n\nSecondly, we show the comparison between models trained on general word embeddings, word embedding + character-level embedding, word embedding + part-of-speech(POS) one-hot encoding and word embedding + grapheme clustered or sub-word embedding.\n\nmentioned in Table TABREF30.\n\nAs, we slowly increase the dropout rate, the F1 score also gradually increases, however after dropout rate = 0.5, the F1 score starts falling down.\n\nEvaluation\tIn this section, we present the details regarding evaluation and comparison of our models with other baselines.\n\nWe can deduce that Skip Gram models perform better compared CBOW models for word2vec and fasttext.\n\nFrom this table TABREF25, we can clearly observe that model using fastText_Skip Gram embeddings outperforms all other models.\n\nTable TABREF35 shows the model architecture comparison between all the models experimented.",
